cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below. A journal article is in preparation."
type: software
title: "ANKYRA: anchoring month-ahead load forecasters to each unit's own history, and when the combination is worth making"
abstract: >-
  In month-ahead load forecasting, the monthly-level error of several kinds of forecaster can be compensated from the
  unit's own long history. The adaptation needs no retraining or fine-tuning of the forecaster (the carrier), and
  whether the combination goes on to improve on a history-only forecast depends on the complementary information the
  carrier supplies. ANKYRA is the tool that implements this finding for buildings, industrial meters and households.
  It takes the forecasts of an existing forecaster (zero-shot TimesFM 2.5 in the released configuration), estimates
  the combination weights from the unit's errors at its own completed pseudo-forecast origins, and returns the hourly
  trajectory of the next 744 hours, the month's energy, the peak and a prediction interval. An exact decomposition of
  the trajectory into monthly level, daily path and within-day shape serves as a diagnostic record. The repository
  contains the package, its tests and exact properties, the evaluation evidence (scored results against 20
  forecasters on ten populations and four external populations, and comparisons across carriers from two
  foundation-model families and two trained models), and the code that regenerates every figure.
